    {
      "id": "review",
      "title": "#412 · bulk discount tiers",
      "lead": "**Request changes.** The design is right: tiers apply per line, before the coupon and before VAT.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "md": "`tierFor` picks the highest tier first, `applyCoupon` now sums tiered line totals, and `priceOrder` reports what the customer saved. The boundary check and the money type are wrong, and the tests stop short of both boundaries."
        },
        {
          "type": "checklist",
          "id": "findings",
          "title": "Findings · #412",
          "numbered": false,
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "tier-boundary",
              "text": "Fix: an order of exactly 10 or 50 units gets no tier",
              "state": "blocker · high",
              "stateKind": "risk",
              "detail": "**File:** `src/pricing/tiers.ts:17`\n\nThe spec says \"10 or more\" and \"50 or more\". `qty > t.minQty` excludes both thresholds: 10 units get no discount, 50 units get 5 % instead of 10 %.\n\n**Suggested fix:** `qty >= t.minQty`."
            },
            {
              "id": "float-cents",
              "text": "Fix: tiered line totals are fractional cents",
              "state": "major · high",
              "stateKind": "warn",
              "detail": "**File:** `src/pricing/tiers.ts:25`\n\n`gross * (1 - tier.percent / 100)` returns 3,163.5 for 3 × 1,110 cents at 5 %. `applyCoupon` rounds only when a coupon is present, so without one the fraction reaches `addTax` and the payment request.\n\n**Suggested fix:** `Math.round(gross * (100 - tier.percent) / 100)`, the same form `applyCoupon` uses."
            },
            {
              "id": "savings-includes-coupon",
              "text": "Fix: `bulkSavingsCents` also counts the coupon",
              "state": "major · medium",
              "stateKind": "warn",
              "detail": "**File:** `src/orders/createOrder.ts:16`\n\nThe savings figure is gross-with-tax minus final total, so a 15 % coupon shows up as bulk savings on the receipt.\n\n**Suggested fix:** compute savings from `lineTotal` alone: `sum(gross) - sum(lineTotal)`, then add tax."
            },
            {
              "id": "boundary-tests",
              "text": "Add tests at 9, 10, 49 and 50 units",
              "state": "minor · high",
              "stateKind": "info",
              "detail": "**File:** `test/tiers.test.ts:5-11`\n\nThe tests check 5 and 60 units, so they pass with the off-by-one above. Boundary cases would have caught it."
            },
            {
              "id": "docs-stale",
              "text": "Update `docs/pricing.md`, which still says there are no bulk discounts",
              "state": "minor · high",
              "stateKind": "info",
              "detail": "**File:** `docs/pricing.md:11` (not changed by this PR)\n\nAdd tiers to the order of operations: sum lines, apply tiers, apply coupon, add VAT."
            },
            {
              "id": "pr-claims-tests",
              "text": "Fix the PR description: it says every tier is tested",
              "state": "nit · high",
              "stateKind": "todo",
              "detail": "The description says \"tests cover every tier\"; only the 10 % tier has a positive test."
            }
          ]
        },
